# A `__gc` finalizer runs with Lua's hooks switched off — when a reload
# closes the state, at quit, or mid-collection — so the budget could
# never cut one that loops: `script.reload` hung the UI thread for good.
# `setmetatable` refuses a metatable with `__gc`; the line that asks is
# the script's error, and reloading stays safe.
write .mnml/init.lua "mnml.command{ id = 'ok', run = function() mnml.toast('STILL-ALIVE') end }\nKEEP = setmetatable({}, { __gc = function() while true do end end })\n"
command script.reload
expect screen contains "__gc"
command user.ok
expect screen contains "STILL-ALIVE"
command script.reload
command user.ok
expect screen contains "STILL-ALIVE"
